cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this paper, the operation taxonomy, or the audit, please
  cite it as below.
title: "From Scores to Knowledge Work: Rethinking AI Agent Evaluation"
abstract: >-
  Knowledge work accounts for a large share of value in advanced
  economies and is a central target for current AI-agent deployment.
  We argue that high scores on public benchmarks under-determine
  readiness for knowledge work, and propose evaluating agents on
  cross-job operations under two audit axes: coverage (whether the
  evaluation exercises the operations the deployment claim is about)
  and validity (whether the score supports the intended use of the
  output, separated into task validity and organizational validity).
  We instantiate the framework with an 18-operation taxonomy derived
  from O*NET 30.2, externally checked against ESCO v1.1.1, and audit
  three frontier suites (GDPval, tau^2-Bench, APEX-Agents) against a
  strict-cover rule and the validity criteria.
